      ⍝ Regression

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ random numbers differ between interpreters
      A←?100⍴100
      B←?30⍴100
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      Z1←A∼B      ⍝ 30×100 = 3000 ⇒ small argument algorithm
      Z2←A∼B,B    ⍝ 30×100 = 3000 ⇒ large argument algorithm
      Z1≡Z2
1

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #3, 2026-08-06): A∼B (and other
      ⍝ primitives that allocate a worst-case ravel and then shrink the
      ⍝ shape in place, e.g. Quad_RE.cc, Bif_F12_COMMA.cc, Quad_FIO.cc,
      ⍝ Bif_F12_FORMAT.cc, Bif_F12_TAKE_DROP.cc, Quad_TF.cc,
      ⍝ Bif_OPER2_RANK.cc, Bif_F12_PARTITION_PICK.cc, PrimitiveFunction.cc)
      ⍝ used to make ~Value() deallocate using nz_element_count() (the
      ⍝ current, post-shrink count) instead of the count actually passed
      ⍝ to allocate() -- sized-deallocation UB (confirmed via ASan
      ⍝ new-delete-type-mismatch on this exact expression: "size of the
      ⍝ allocated type: 2400 bytes; size of the deallocated type: 2328
      ⍝ bytes"), and total_ravel_count (⎕SYL[6;2]) leaking by exactly the
      ⍝ number of dropped elements every call. Verify the leak is gone:
      ⍝ ⎕SYL[6;2] must be identical before and after 1000 calls that each
      ⍝ drop 3 elements.
      ⍝
      X←(⍳100)∼30 40 50
      before←⎕SYL[6;2]
      ⊣{⊣(⍳100)∼30 40 50 ⋄ ⍵+1}⍣1000⊢0
      before=⎕SYL[6;2]
1

